--- body ---
The forge-ref parser (`parseRef` / `BlockedByRefs` in `ticket.go`) is the
trickiest logic in the codebase: it must accept valid forge refs, reject the
deprecated `gh:` and bare `gh#N` schemes, enforce owner/repo naming rules, and
handle case variants. It is currently covered only by one case in
`validate_test.go` and 10 shell cases in `test_validate.sh`.

A dedicated `TestParseRef` table test in `ticket_test.go` would:
- Pin each accepted and rejected ref pattern with a precise error substring
- Run without spawning subprocesses
- Be the first thing that fails when the regex is changed

Minimum cases to cover:
- Valid: `github.com/owner/repo#1`, `gitlab.com/g/p/sub#42`
- Rejected deprecated: `gh:owner/repo#1`, `gh#123`
- Rejected malformed: missing `#`, zero issue number, numeric owner,
  uppercase in path component (if enforced), missing repo
- Edge: two `Blocked-by:` lines on same ticket (both parsed)
